From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PROPOSED] winedmo: report irreversible seek failures to MediaEngine

Review overlay against the final A3.19 Wine tree. Fold into a fresh candidate's
terminal-error patch after review; no historical pin or artifact is changed.

A non-progressive avformat_seek_file() failure returns STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL.
After the old timeline has been flushed, media_source_start() stops the demux
thread and retains that failure, but MediaSession and MediaEngine recognize
only cancellation and network errors. The source's generic MEError is lost,
leaving the pending session start and engine seek unresolved.

Normalize only this irreversible post-flush seek failure to
MF_E_INVALID_POSITION, retaining the original numeric error in a warning.
Publish it through the existing first-error-wins helper and admit that one
additional status through the current-source error route. Map it to DECODE,
not NETWORK: failure to establish the requested media position does not
identify a transport failure. Cancellation and known network codes retain
their existing meanings. Synchronous argument rejection before flushing is
unchanged.

Keep source identity/generation checks, one user-visible error per source,
command completion without a successful Started/Seeked event, and manual
SetSource/reopen recovery. No EOF synthesis, automatic retry, new channel,
or generic failed-MEError forwarding is added. This closes a source-proven
error-propagation gap, not a proven cause of the episode #331 stalls.

The licenses of the modified Wine source files apply to this patch.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -1359,19 +1359,16 @@ static HRESULT media_source_start(struct media_source *source, IMFPresentationDescriptor *descriptor,
             /* Cancellation or seek failed after the old queues were flushed.
              * Keep the epoch odd and stop the producer rather than retrying an
              * unknown or damaged timeline. */
-            if (error == MF_E_OPERATION_CANCELLED || error == MF_E_NET_TIMEOUT
-                    || error == MF_E_NET_READ)
+            if (error != MF_E_OPERATION_CANCELLED && error != MF_E_NET_TIMEOUT
+                    && error != MF_E_NET_READ)
             {
-                *error_queued = media_source_queue_demux_error(source, error);
-                if (!*error_queued && error_event_generation != InterlockedCompareExchange(
-                        &source->demux_error_event_generation, 0, 0))
-                    *error_queued = TRUE;
-            }
-            else
-            {
-                source->demux_thread_shutdown = true;
-                media_source_set_demux_error(source, error);
+                WARN("Failed to establish seek position, original error %#lx; stopping source.\n", error);
+                error = MF_E_INVALID_POSITION;
             }
+            *error_queued = media_source_queue_demux_error(source, error);
+            if (!*error_queued && error_event_generation != InterlockedCompareExchange(
+                    &source->demux_error_event_generation, 0, 0))
+                *error_queued = TRUE;
             for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
             {
                 struct media_stream *stream = source->streams[i];
diff --git a/dlls/mf/session.c b/dlls/mf/session.c
--- a/dlls/mf/session.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/session.c
@@ -4881,7 +4881,7 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI session_events_callback_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *iface, IMFAsyncResult *result)
                 if (hr == MF_E_SHUTDOWN)
                     session_handle_source_shutdown(session);
                 else if (hr == MF_E_OPERATION_CANCELLED || hr == MF_E_NET_TIMEOUT
-                        || hr == MF_E_NET_READ)
+                        || hr == MF_E_NET_READ || hr == MF_E_INVALID_POSITION)
                 {
                     if (!(session_source->flags & SOURCE_FLAG_TERMINAL_ERROR_FORWARDED))
                     {
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1212,7 +1212,7 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_session_events_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *iface, IMFAsyncResult *result)
 
             if (FAILED(IMFMediaEvent_GetStatus(event, &error)) ||
                     (error != MF_E_OPERATION_CANCELLED && error != MF_E_NET_TIMEOUT
-                    && error != MF_E_NET_READ) ||
+                    && error != MF_E_NET_READ && error != MF_E_INVALID_POSITION) ||
                     FAILED(IMFMediaEvent_GetValue(event, &source)) ||
                     source.vt != VT_UNKNOWN || !source.punkVal)
             {
@@ -1220,8 +1220,12 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_session_events_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *iface, IMFAsyncResult *result)
                 break;
             }
 
-            error_code = error == MF_E_OPERATION_CANCELLED
-                    ? MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_ERR_ABORTED : MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_ERR_NETWORK;
+            if (error == MF_E_OPERATION_CANCELLED)
+                error_code = MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_ERR_ABORTED;
+            else if (error == MF_E_INVALID_POSITION)
+                error_code = MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_ERR_DECODE;
+            else
+                error_code = MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_ERR_NETWORK;
             EnterCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
             if ((engine->flags & FLAGS_ENGINE_SHUT_DOWN)
                     || engine->presentation.generation != engine->source_generation
